{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-17 08:20:59 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-17 15:20:59 +0700\n\nReviewed the complete revision against HEAD `5f8963093631ab447840cd6a041d83fadccf3999`; tracked files match HEAD. No files edited. This was specification and Zend-source inspection; PHP CLI fixtures were not executed.\n\nThe supported-fragment approach is appropriate. Saved evidence cursors, late acquisition, ordinary copy-during-iteration, non-vivifying missing-path unset, resurrection and shutdown-global preservation are addressed. Three defects remain **inside the claimed fragment**:\n\n1. **[P1] Argument ownership must be acquired during argument evaluation, not at call entry.**  \n   [Row 39](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792223000000-architect-ts-php-r6.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:79) postpones rows 33/34 until the call begins:\n   ```php\n   function f($x, $unused) { echo $x[0]; }\n   $a = [1]; $r =& $a[0]; unset($r);\n   f($a, $a[0] = 2); // PHP: 1\n   ```\n   Zend captures the first argument and acquires its array ownership before evaluating the second. Delayed acquisition leaves the table singly owned during the write and produces `2`. Pending argument slots need ownership immediately, plus cleanup if later argument evaluation throws. They cannot remain uncounted borrowed values until invocation. [Zend SEND handlers](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_vm_def.h).\n\n2. **[P1] Row 41 gives incorrect uninitialized typed-reference semantics.**  \n   [Row 41](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792223000000-architect-ts-php-r6.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:94) permits a reference holding an uninitialized sentinel:\n   ```php\n   class C { public int $x; }\n   $o = new C;\n   $r =& $o->x; // Error here, before any read through $r\n   ```\n   Zend rejects acquisition from an uninitialized **non-nullable** property. For a nullable property, acquisition initializes it to `null` before wrapping it. Replace the sentinel rule with these branches and their fixtures. This belongs to the specified typed-reference behavior and Phase 3 type enforcement. [Zend reference-fetch validation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_execute.c).\n\n3. **[P1] Iterator migration may require separation after `FE_RESET_RW`.**  \n   [Rows 25–26](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792223000000-architect-ts-php-r6.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:24) omit separation when the iterated reference is assigned a different shared table:\n   ```php\n   $a = [1];\n   $b = [2]; $r =& $b[0]; unset($r);\n   foreach ($a as &$v) {\n       if ($v === 1) $a = $b;\n       else { $v = 3; break; }\n   }\n   echo $b[0]; // PHP: 2\n   ```\n   On migration to an unrelated table, `zend_hash_iterator_pos_ex` separates that table when shared. The proposed reset-to-zero plus non-separating fetch instead modifies `$b`, producing `3`. Preserve the distinction between ordinary element fetch and iterator migration, including iterator-copy tracking. C15 explicitly keeps whole-array assignment in row 26, so this is not a deferred rebuilding-builtin corner. [Zend iterator migration](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_hash.c).\n\nTwo support-profile refinements are also needed:\n\n4. **[P2] Clone’s reference-copy rule is sound, but readonly reinitialization is unclassified.**  \n   [Row 52](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792223000000-architect-ts-php-r6.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:126) correctly unwraps count-one references and retains shared references. PHP 8.3 additionally permits readonly-property reinitialization during `__clone`, using temporary reinitialization flags. Specify that behavior or add a named unsupported/restricted corner; the current corner list does not identify it. [Zend clone implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_objects.c).\n\n5. **[P2] The convergence rule must still block defects in claimed rows.**  \n   [B.3](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792223000000-architect-ts-php-r6.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:174) says only missing required rows block. A known incorrect row within the published support profile must also block until corrected or explicitly excluded. Future oracle fixtures cannot make a contradictory normative rule sound.\n\nThe corner table can support convergence without implementing all of Zend. The outstanding blockers concern ordinary argument capture, typed-reference acquisition and array alias preservation already claimed by this design; none requires expanding the fragment.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES"}}
